      say: `Start with what Microsoft gives you. Learn's bulk upload page is the contract: a SCIM post to the provisioning job, at most fifty user operations a request and forty requests a second. The service matches on the attributes the job maps, resolves the manager, and disables the user when a record sends active false. A successful call returns accepted, with a header pointing to the provisioning logs. For recertification, an assignment policy's review settings carry reviewers, a schedule, and what happens when nobody responds.`,
      detail: `Learn's Perform bulkUpload page is the contract: POST /servicePrincipals/{servicePrincipalId}/synchronization/jobs/{jobId}/bulkUpload with Content-Type: application/scim+json, at most 50 user operations per request and a rate limit of 40 requests per second. The provisioning service matches on the attributes the job maps (externalId in the examples) to create, update, enable or disable the account, resolves manager.value as the manager's externalId, and disables the user when a record sends active false. A successful call returns 202 Accepted with a Location header that points to the provisioning logs. The least-privileged application permission is SynchronizationData-User.Upload.OwnedBy; SynchronizationData-User.Upload is the higher one and the only delegated one, for a User Administrator. For recertification, the reviewSettings of an access package assignment policy carry isEnabled, primaryReviewers, fallbackReviewers, schedule and expirationBehavior, whose values are keepAccess, removeAccess and acceptAccessRecommendation. Learn's procedure for a review of an access package offers monthly, quarterly, bi-annual and annual frequencies, Manager as reviewer with a fallback, and the no-response choices no change, remove access or take recommendations.`,
