      say: `Two sets of rules sit around that computation. The source checks quarantine a record with no contract end, or whose sponsor isn't in the HR export, warn when a sponsor has separated, and note an engagement ending within two weeks. The reconciliation compares the register, the card system and the directory: an enabled account past its end, an orphan account, a card for someone the register doesn't hold, a record with no account, and a leave date that isn't the earliest end. It's read only, joined on the person key.`,
      detail: `CS-01 Finding: no contract end date; quarantined (the guide: an enforced earliest end). CS-02 Finding: sponsor not in the HR export; quarantined, no manager (the evaluation's mapping: the sponsor as manager). CS-03 Warn: sponsor separated; access ends after the grace period unless a new sponsor is recorded (Appendix A). CS-04 Info: an engagement ending within 14 days (design guidance). CR-01 Finding: an enabled account past its earliest end (Appendix A). CR-02 Finding: an enabled contractor account with no register record, orphan (Book 03, Chapter 11). CR-03 Finding: an active card for a person the register doesn't hold (Book 03, Chapter 11: contractor credential drift). CR-04 Warn: an active register record with no account (design guidance). CR-05 Finding: employeeLeaveDateTime that isn't the earliest end (design guidance: the leaver fires on the wrong day). The reconciliation is read only, joined on the enterprise person key in employeeId, as the guide's step 2 asks before anything changes.`,
