      say: `The verified facts, each read on November first. Bulk upload is a version one point oh API: fifty operations a request, forty requests a second, and an accepted response pointing to the logs. Its least permission is the owned-by upload permission. The review settings and the access review procedure are both documented, and access reviews are available in Azure Government. The requestor manager subject set is documented for approval stages. And the policy update cmdlet needs the entitlement management read-write permission.`,
      detail: `Perform bulkUpload: POST /servicePrincipals/{id}/synchronization/jobs/{jobId}/bulkUpload; application/scim+json; 50 operations per request; 40 requests per second; 202 Accepted with a Location header to the provisioning logs; no national cloud table on the page; API-driven inbound provisioning listed as available in Azure Government; v1.0. bulkUpload permissions: application SynchronizationData-User.Upload.OwnedBy (least), SynchronizationData-User.Upload; delegated SynchronizationData-User.Upload, for a User Administrator; v1.0. Matching and state: matching attributes per the job's mapping; active false disables; manager.value is the manager's externalId; v1.0. Review settings: isEnabled, primaryReviewers, fallbackReviewers, schedule, expirationBehavior (keepAccess, removeAccess, acceptAccessRecommendation); access reviews available in Azure Government; v1.0. Access review of a package (procedure): monthly, quarterly, bi-annual or annual; Manager as reviewer with a fallback; no response: no change, remove access or take recommendations; GA. requestorManager: a subject set for a requestor's manager, managerLevel 1 or 2, documented for approval stages; v1.0. Update an assignment policy: Set-MgEntitlementManagementAssignmentPolicy, EntitlementManagement.ReadWrite.All; v1.0. List users with leave date: User.Read.All with User-LifeCycleInfo.Read.All; v1.0; carried from the validation kit's VK-HR-05.`,
