      detail: `You need Python 3.10 or later. Work in examples/hr-lifecycle. Step 1: python python/graph_export.py --task contractor-reconcile --list prints Task contractor-reconcile: User-LifeCycleInfo.Read.All, User.Read.All and GET /users. Step 2: python python/contractor_source.py extract --register tests/fixtures/ch02/contractor-register.csv --cards tests/fixtures/ch02/cards.csv --sponsors tests/fixtures/ch02/hr-sponsors.csv --rules config/contractor-rules.json --as-of 2026-11-01 --out out/ch02/extract prints Contractors: 9 records: 3 active, 4 inactive (past their earliest end), 2 quarantined; Source: 2 Finding, 1 Warn, 1 Info; the extract written. The exit code is 2, because the run has a Finding or a Warn. Step 3 reads decisions.json: 900007 has no contract end (CS-01); 900008's sponsor isn't in the HR export (CS-02). 900004's sponsor separated on September 30, so the 30-day grace period ends October 30 (CS-03). 900005's card expired October 28, but its sponsor recertification was due October 25, which comes first.`,
