      detail: `Step 4: python ../hcm-entra/python/hcm_to_scim.py --extract out/ch02/extract/contractors-extract.csv --as-of 2026-11-01 --out out/ch02/scim prints {"counts": {"ready": 7}, "batches": 1, "disables": 4, "held": false, "hold_reason": ""}. Seven records in one batch, four of them disables. out/ch02/scim/bulk-request-001.json sends 900002, 900003, 900004 and 900005 with active false. Nothing is sent: the middleware's dry run is its default. Step 5: python python/contractor_source.py reconcile ... --as-of 2026-11-01 --cloud gcc --out out/ch02/reconcile prints Reconciliation: 7 Finding, 1 Warn, 0 Info (exit code 2); the findings: four CR-01 accounts enabled past their earliest end, one CR-02 orphan, one CR-03 card for 900011, one CR-05 leave date 2026-12-10 that isn't the earliest end 2026-11-10, one CR-04 register record with no account. The four CR-01 accounts are the four disables in step 4: once the requests are sent, the next reconciliation shows none, which is the guide's evidence for the gate. (The slide shows the capture's output lines; the full commands are in the chapter.)`,
