      say: `Lab 2 uses a test tenant; the authors haven't run it. Set up the contractor provisioning app, and grant the middleware the owned-by upload permission on that app only. Send two test contractors, one active and one past its end, and read the provisioning logs. Reconcile against the tenant: there should be no finding for the account you just disabled. Then apply the review settings by merging them into the policy you read back, and confirm the reviewer is the manager. Finally, restore the policy and clean up.`,
      detail: `Not run by the authors. Use a test tenant in the worldwide or GCC cloud, never production. You'll need my-register.csv, my-cards.csv and my-sponsors.csv in the layout of tests/fixtures/ch02. 1 Set up the contractor provisioning app as Learn's API-driven inbound provisioning procedure describes, with the attribute mappings examples/hcm-entra documents, and grant the middleware's identity SynchronizationData-User.Upload.OwnedBy on that app only. 2 Send two test contractors through the middleware's apply path, as Book 19, Chapter 01's Lab 2 describes: one active, one past its end. Read the provisioning log entry each Location header points to, and confirm the second account is disabled and both carry the leave date. 3 Reconcile against the tenant, with a token in HRLC_GRAPH_TOKEN for an app holding User.Read.All and User-LifeCycleInfo.Read.All: there should be no CR-01 for the account step 2 disabled. 4 Apply the review settings to a test contractor package: read the policy back into policy-before.json, merge reviewSettings into policy-new.json, review it, send it with Set-MgEntitlementManagementAssignmentPolicy, and read the primary reviewers back. If the service refuses requestorManager as a reviewer, set Manager as reviewer in the admin center as Learn's procedure shows, export the policy, and record the subject set it uses. 5 Back it out: restore the policy's previous reviewSettings from your read-back; pause the provisioning job (a paused job keeps its state), delete the test contractors, and remove the permissions; delete the lab's output folders and policy files.`,
